Third-party components
======================

Bundled as dependencies of the plugin (resolved from Maven Central):

- commonmark-java 0.31.0 (org.commonmark:commonmark and the GFM tables, strikethrough,
  task list items and autolink extensions) - BSD 2-Clause License,
  https://github.com/commonmark/commonmark-java
- jsoup 1.16.1 (org.jsoup:jsoup) - MIT License, https://jsoup.org
- kotlinx.serialization 1.7.1 (org.jetbrains.kotlinx:kotlinx-serialization-json) -
  Apache License 2.0, https://github.com/Kotlin/kotlinx.serialization

Resolved by the plugin at build time in the project that applies it (not contained in this
repository or in the plugin artifact):

- PlantUML, MIT-licensed build (net.sourceforge.plantuml:plantuml-mit) - MIT License,
  https://plantuml.com
- @plantuml/core (npm package, the browser build of PlantUML) - MIT License. The site copies
  these files of the package into its output:
  - plantuml.js, emoji.js, openiconic.js, LICENSE - MIT License;
  - viz-global.js - Viz.js 3.24.0, MIT License, Copyright (c) Michael Daines; it contains
    in object code form Graphviz (Eclipse Public License 1.0, https://www.graphviz.org) and
    Expat (MIT License, https://libexpat.github.io);
  - themes.js - the PlantUML themes; each theme states its own license in its header
    (MIT, Apache License 2.0, and GPL 3+ for the "sunlust" theme). The themes are data that
    PlantUML reads only when a diagram selects a theme with `!theme`.
- Dokka command line and plugins (org.jetbrains.dokka:dokka-cli, dokka-base,
  templating-plugin, all-modules-page-plugin, analysis-kotlin-symbols) -
  Apache License 2.0, https://github.com/Kotlin/dokka
- rumdl, the Markdown linter (a native binary) - MIT License, Copyright (c) 2024-2025 Ruben J. Jongejan,
  https://github.com/rvben/rumdl. The plugin is not distributed with rumdl: the lint tasks
  download the release archive of the platform from the rumdl releases or a configured
  mirror into the Gradle user home and run it as a separate process. The archive contains
  the LICENSE of rumdl; only the binary is extracted.

The site does not use any network resources at run time: fonts are the system fonts of the
reader, and the scripts and styles of the site are part of this repository.
